# Test: data-rm-refused-live
# VALIDATES: AC-3 (local half), AC-4 (delete), AC-5 (delete) -- the local `ze data rm` on the daemon's host, while the daemon owns the store, sends the removal to the daemon: a runtime-state key seeded while ze was stopped is removed with the local route's lines (`removed <key>`, `1 entries removed from <store>`) and exit 0, and a fresh reader handle no longer finds it; removing it again is an error, exit 2; a configuration key is refused naming why; the key of the running ddos-flowspec plugin is refused naming `request plugin restart ddos-flowspec`.
# PREVENTS: a `ze data rm` that needs ze stopped, a daemon removal that prints other lines than the local one, a removal of a running plugin's state from under it.
# QUESTION: does the local command, refused the store by the owner lock, reach the daemon over SSH with the login of the daemon's host and print what the local route prints? A unit test stubs the daemon (TestDataRmForwardsToDaemonWhenBusy) and cannot see the lock, the address and login resolution, the dispatcher or the running plugin.
# RUNNING PLUGIN: ddos-flowspec, configured at `response-level alert`, which needs no BGP peer, no detection and no kernel feature. Its grant is meta/ddos-flowspec/announcement (internal/plugins/ddos/flowspec/register.go). The key is never written here, so its refusal proves the guard runs before the store is touched.

option=storage:value=disk
option=timeout:value=90s

tmpfs=stale.txt:terminator=EOF_STALE
stale runtime state
EOF_STALE

tmpfs=data-rm-refused-live.conf:terminator=EOF_CONF
system {
    authentication {
        user admin {
            password "$2a$04$UlwuiuH82Unfsq.XEMPGJeDkXwbm3KW.nvVaVXOd/JeFK8VjMjrQO"
        }
    }
}

environment {
    ssh {
        enabled true
        server main {
            ip 127.0.0.1;
            port $PORT2;
        }
    }
}

ddos {
    flowspec {
        response-level alert
        action discard
    }
}

bgp {
    router-id 1.2.3.4
    session {
        asn {
            local 65000
        }
    }
}
EOF_CONF

# The first start creates the store; the key is seeded while ze is stopped,
# the only time the offline writer may open it.
cmd=background:seq=1:exec=ze start data-rm-refused-live.conf:name=first:ready=Ze running.
cmd=stop:seq=2:name=first:signal=term
cmd=foreground:seq=3:exec=ze data write meta/test/stale-state stale.txt:exit=0
cmd=background:seq=4:exec=ze start data-rm-refused-live.conf:name=daemon:ready=Ze running.
cmd=foreground:seq=5:exec=le test fixture storage/data-rm-refused-live $PORT2:exit=0
expect=stdout:contains=OK: data-rm-refused-live
cmd=stop:seq=6:name=daemon:signal=term
